  "slug": "hvac-rooftop-unit-cleaning-checklist-form",
  "title": "HVAC Rooftop Unit Cleaning and Restoration Checklist",
  "subtitle": "Plan, perform, verify, and close out rooftop-unit cleaning while controlling electrical, chemical, roof, water, and contamination hazards and preserving a defensible record of methods, findings, readings, evidence, and restoration.",
  "description": "A field-ready HVAC rooftop unit cleaning checklist covering asset identity, authorization, pre-clean condition, isolation, products and methods, coil and drain work, cabinet and airside cleaning, waste control, post-clean verification, defect escalation, and accountable return to service.",
  "use_case": "Use for scheduled or condition-driven RTU cleaning when a facility or service provider needs one fillable record showing what was cleaned, how it was protected, which products were used, what changed, which defects remain, and who authorized normal operation.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
